# Examples live in MetaMetro

Example graphs, reads, colourings, and ground truth live in **MetaMetro 0.17.1** (`312070ada1e310ff1ca321ff1e509debd9d05495`, https://github.com/dsmutin/metaMetro). They do not live in this repository.

Build them from that checkout. A fresh checkout has an empty `data/bench`; `benchbuild` fills it:

```bash
metametro benchbuild --all
metametro benchbuild bubble_strain_2
```

BubbleBlower only runs a loader against that build:

```python
load_bench_graph("bubble_strain_2", namespaces=("taxon",))
```

Do not commit the build. That includes MetaMetro `data/bench/` and a second copy under `examples/*/data` (CFA, CDBG, unitigs, links, reads, ground truth, or metrics written from a local bench). If the bench directory is missing, run `benchbuild`. Do not paste a local graph in its place.

A tiny graph that exists only inside one test file may stay in that test. It is not an example.
